From Gilbert.Ritschard at unige.ch  Tue May 29 18:35:18 2012
From: Gilbert.Ritschard at unige.ch (Gilbert Ritschard)
Date: Tue, 29 May 2012 18:35:18 +0200
Subject: [Traminer-users] seqefsub
In-Reply-To: <20120529161729.298160@gmx.net>
References: <20120529161729.298160@gmx.net>
Message-ID: <4FC4FAC6.90902@unige.ch>

Sandra,

Glad to learn that you are using TraMineR for your PhD,

With 225 events in a sequence there much too many subsequence, which 
causes the crash.

The solution is to limit the length of the subsequences that TraMineR 
should search for.
You do that with the maxK argument of the seqefsub function, e.g. by setting

maxK=5

Hope this helps.

Good luck.
Gilbert


